# Supabase CLI local cache (linked project, pooler URL, versions)
supabase/.temp/
.wrangler/

# ⚠️ ROOT-LEVEL SCRATCH. THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC.
# `supabase/.temp/` above has been ignored for a long time and reads as though it covers
# scratch generally. It does not — it is anchored to that one subdirectory, so a `.temp/`
# at the repo root was fully trackable, and a single `git add -A` from any session would
# have published whatever was in it. It has in practice accumulated fetched page blobs,
# wrangler logs, one-off patch scripts and working notes that quote account state and
# tenant configuration — none of which belongs in a public repo.
# Working notes that are worth keeping belong in the Obsidian vault, not here.
.temp/

# Dev tooling (preflight gate)
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# Written by `deno check --node-modules-dir=none`, which CLAUDE.md tells everyone to
# run on the edge functions — so it reappears for every contributor. Not committed:
# the functions are deployed by the Supabase CLI, which resolves independently, and
# there is no build step for this lock to make reproducible.
deno.lock

# The walk-around clip dev/verify-cal3d.mjs generates with ffmpeg on first run. Not
# committed: dev/ ships in the Workers asset bundle, so a checked-in 113KB video would be a
# public download on every tenant site to serve one local harness.
dev/scan-fixtures/walk-around-stub.mp4
dev/scan-fixtures/big-photo.jpg

# ⚠️ THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC. A scoring corpus entry carries a measured truth, the priors
# it is scored against, the drafts already recorded and the timestamp each run fired at —
# and nothing else. No tenant id, no style key, no frame URLs, and no ai_style_calls row
# ids: eight of those were committed with the corpus and taken back out on 2026-09-19. They
# were read by nothing (scoreEntry consumes drafted, observed, source, dims and label) and
# they are production primary keys, which is not a thing to publish for no reason. What a
# LIVE or --replay run needs lives beside the entry in <entry>.local.json, which never
# leaves the machine.
dev/score-corpus/*.local.json
